From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vtkOpenGLRenderWindow: Do not query the sizes of a missing color attachment

GetColorBufferSizes queries the red, green, blue and alpha sizes of the draw
buffer of the bound draw framebuffer. While a QVTKOpenGLNativeWidget
initializes, the context is current on Qt's offscreen surface; on Wayland
that surface has no color buffer, so the attachment (GL_BACK_LEFT of the
default framebuffer) has the object type GL_NONE. Mesa then raises
GL_INVALID_OPERATION for each size, and VTK warns four times ("Failed to get
red color buffer size (1282)" and the same for green, blue and alpha), which
ParaView shows in its Output Messages window whenever a view is flat. On X11
the offscreen surface has a color buffer and nothing is reported.

Read the attachment's object type first, as GetDepthBufferSize does for
the depth attachment since "Do not query a missing depth attachment": with no
attachment the sizes are 0, which is what the failed queries left before, so
the alpha bit planes stay as they were (0 on Wayland, 8 on X11). An error from
the object type query itself falls through to the existing queries and their
warnings.

Bug: Output Messages window on Wayland when a ParaView view is flat (ParaView 6.1.1, VTK 9.6.2)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLRenderWindow.cxx
+++ b/Rendering/OpenGL2/vtkOpenGLRenderWindow.cxx
@@ -1118,6 +1118,17 @@
     {
     }
 
+    // A default framebuffer can have no color buffer at all: Qt's offscreen surface on Wayland, current
+    // while a QOpenGLWidget initializes, has none. Querying the size of a missing attachment is a GL error,
+    // so without one the sizes are 0.
+    GLint attachmentType = GL_NONE;
+    glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv(
+      GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment, GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_OBJECT_TYPE, &attachmentType);
+    if (glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR && attachmentType == GL_NONE)
+    {
+      return 0;
+    }
+
     glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv(
       GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment, GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_RED_SIZE, &size);
     if (auto error = glGetError())
